From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:43:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: pmic_pdcharger_ulog: add the SoCCP channel

On SoCs where the battery and USB-C firmware runs on the SoCCP instead
of the ADSP, such as Kaanapali, the firmware offers its log on the
"PMIC_LOGS_SOCCP_APPS" channel, just as pmic_glink itself uses
"PMIC_RTR_SOCCP_APPS" there. The messages are the same. Match that
channel too.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_pdcharger_ulog.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_pdcharger_ulog.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_pdcharger_ulog.c
index 39f412bbf2c1..50f52ca757de 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_pdcharger_ulog.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_pdcharger_ulog.c
@@ -148,6 +148,7 @@ static void pmic_pdcharger_ulog_rpmsg_remove(struct rpmsg_device *rpdev)
 
 static const struct rpmsg_device_id pmic_pdcharger_ulog_rpmsg_id_match[] = {
 	{ "PMIC_LOGS_ADSP_APPS" },
+	{ "PMIC_LOGS_SOCCP_APPS" },
 	{}
 };
 /*
